# The Pad is one file, served at every URL that used to have its own copy.
#
# index.html at the repo root is the real file — the front door is never a
# redirect, so if this file is ever missing or wrong, / still serves.
#
# 200 = rewrite: the browser's URL is unchanged, the root index.html is served.
# That is why index.html fetches /catalog.json absolutely; a relative path
# would resolve to a different place at each of the URLs below.
#
# Exact paths only — no wildcards. /pad/* would otherwise shadow /pad/media/.
# (Netlify applies these rules only when no static file matches, so the media
# is safe either way, but exact rules keep that from being load-bearing.)
#
# The .html and /pad/catalog.json rules exist because the old deploy served
# those URLs as real files. They are kept so nothing that ever worked 404s.

/pad/catalog.json    /catalog.json    200

/library             /                200
/library.html        /                200
/pad                 /                200
/pad/                /                200
/pad/index.html      /                200
